# Each field has the width of what the program stores in it: the double and the string a word each, the count 32 bits, the owner, which is only ever null, one byte.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="make" role=ResultWrapper
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK: Int32, Double, Int64, Int64 b@[[fields]] = Patchpoint({{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[count]] = Extract(b@[[fields]], <<0,
# CHECK-NEXT: Double b@[[step]] = Extract(b@[[fields]], <<1,
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[owner]] = Extract(b@[[fields]], <<3,
# The string is read from the table of the strings of the image. The first read finds the entry empty and makes it, on a rare path.
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[made]] = Load(b@{{*}}, offset = {{*}}, ControlDependent|Reads:AOTInstance_stringCells, {{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[made]], Terminal,
# CHECK-NEXT: Successors: Then:#{{*}}, Else:Rare:#
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[label]] = Phi(
# CHECK: Int64 b@[[counter]] = Patchpoint(${{*}}(b@{{*}}):Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ControlDependent{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[count]], b@[[counter]], offset = 32, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[step]], b@[[counter]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Store(b@[[label]], b@[[counter]], offset = 24, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[narrow]] = Trunc(b@[[owner]],
# CHECK-NEXT: Store8(b@[[narrow]], b@[[counter]], offset = 36, ControlDependent|Writes:ObjectFields{{*}}:NewObject)
# CHECK: Return(b@[[counter]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# The function that holds the initializers is inlined, and each field is stored once.
# NONE-LABEL: name="make" role=ResultWrapper
# NONE-NOT: :PutSlot
# NONE-NOT: Reads:JSCell
# NONE-NOT: Reads:ModuleVariables
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# CALLS: f1: size=
# CALLS-NEXT: function f{{*}} x1
# CALLS: stub AllocateCell.HeaderAndWords.n3 x1
# CALLS-NOT: stub AllocateCell
# CALLS: f{{*}}: size=
# The four values are constants, and this half still gets them by a call of the other half.
# X64: instructions: 13, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 3
# ARM64: instructions: 14, patchpoints: 2, rare instructions: 5
